6. This Court has considered following aspects;
(i) The applicant is not the one, who has lended the amount to the complainant;
(ii) even as per the FIR, the present applicant is an employee of main accused i.e. Pranav Trivedi;
(iii) the only allegation in the entire FIR against the present applicant is that he has slapped the complainant twice and abuse him;
(iv) there is no past antecedents against the present applicant as submitted by the learned advocate for the applicant.

The applicant is ordered to be released on bail in the event of their arrest in connection with FIR being C.R.No.11196026230044 of 2023 registered with Ravpura Police Station, Dist. Vadodara City on executing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand Only) with one surety of like amount on the following conditions:
R/CR.MA/5976/2023 ORDER DATED: 20/04/2023 Mayur Jagdishbhai Rohit vs State Of Gujarat on 20 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/12055320/
2 (a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make himself available for interrogation whenever required;

( b) shall remain present at concerned Police Station on 27.04.2023 between 11.00 a.m. and 2.00 p.m.;
(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the address to the investigating officer and the court concerned and shall not change residence till the final disposal of the case till further orders;
(f) shall not leave India without the R/CR.MA/5976/2023 ORDER DATED: 20/04/2023 permission of the concerned trial court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned trial court within a week; and (g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if he considers it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide it on merits;
